.TH "NIAC" "1" "Sep 2026" "NIAC" "NIAC Manual"

.SH NAME
niac-config-edit - Open a configuration in $EDITOR and validate the result


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBniac config edit  [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Open a NIAC configuration file in $EDITOR (falling back to $VISUAL, then vi)
and validate it once the editor exits.

.PP
An edit that leaves the file unparseable or invalid is reported; the file is
left as the editor wrote it so the mistake can be corrected.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for edit


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--storage-keep\fP=500
	Run history records to keep, pruned oldest first on start (0 keeps every run)

.PP
\fB--storage-path\fP=""
	Path to NIAC run history database (default: ~/.niac/niac.db)


.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
  # Edit and validate a scenario
  niac config edit clinic.yaml

  # Use a specific editor for one invocation
  EDITOR=nano niac config edit clinic.yaml
.EE


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBniac-config(1)\fP


